{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '140,177p' src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc; sed -n '301,453p' src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc; sed -n '468,490p' src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc; rg -n 'indexer|index-publication|step-count|:steps|defn eval|defn repl-state|:result|:value|:status' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(defn make-indexer\n  \"The indexer for one session: `observer`, attached to `program-out`\n   beside the evaluator's; `:local`, the complete-retention log its\n   transactions are committed to (dao.space.transactor requires memory-log\n   retention); and `content-store`, the `dao.jing` byte store publications\n   materialize into.  `session-token` is the shell's stable token, recorded\n   as provenance; `publish-opts` reach `transactor/publish!` as-is.\n\n   `after-publish` is `(fn [manifest-address])`, called after a round's\n   manifest is read back from the store and before the round is reported\n   published: the durable store's HEAD write, which is what makes the\n   round durably published (docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md).\n   Nil — the memory store — publishes exactly as before.\n\n   `:allocator` retains only the transactor authority, with its intake\n   detached. `:materialization` retains verified coverage as plain data:\n   `{:cursor c :transactions n :manifest-address a :manifest m :max-t t}`.\n   A round's fresh `:publication` intake, pool and tree builder are dropped\n   at its end; no earlier publication payload is retained.\"\n  [{:keys [observer session-token content-store publish-opts after-publish]}]\n  {:observer observer\n   :local (memory-log)\n   :content-store content-store\n   :session-token session-token\n   :publish-opts publish-opts\n   :after-publish after-publish\n   :next-e datom/first-user-id\n   :transactions 0\n   :published 0\n   :published-payloads 0\n   :manifest-address nil\n   :allocator nil\n   :materialization nil\n   :lost? false\n   :failure nil})\n\n\n(defn- next-entity-id\n(defn- commit\n  \"Commit one packet as one transaction; its rows join `:unwritten`, which\n   the round writes before it publishes (`write-rows`).  A packet that\n   could not be projected or committed is consumed and recorded as the\n   failure, never counted, and materializes nothing.\"\n  [ix packet round]\n  (try\n    (let [{:keys [tx-data next-e root row-set]}\n          (packet->tx-data packet\n                           (:next-e ix)\n                           {:session-token (:session-token ix), :round round})\n          answer (transactor/transact! (get-in ix [:publication :transactor])\n                                       tx-data)]\n      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n        [(-> ix\n             (assoc :next-e next-e)\n             (update :transactions inc)\n             (update :unwritten (fnil conj []) row-set))\n         true]\n        [(assoc ix\n                :failure {:round round\n                          :root root\n                          :stage :transact\n                          :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome answer)})\n         false]))\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n      [(assoc ix\n              :failure {:round round\n                        :stage :project\n                        :message (ex-message e)})\n       false])))\n\n\n(defn- materialize\n  \"Drain the intake into the store until it blocks.  Answers how many\n   payloads it materialized and, when the drain met a gap or a defect, what\n   it met.  The pool is not kept: its intake is dropped with the round.\"\n  [content-store pool]\n  (loop [pool pool\n         n 0]\n    (let [{:keys [signal], :as r} (jing/observe-step! content-store pool)]\n      (case signal\n        :dao.stream/ok\n        (let [missing #?(:cljd (Object.) :clj (Object.) :cljs (js-obj))]\n          ;; Every emitted dirty node reads back before HEAD moves. The\n          ;; unchanged subgraphs were verified by earlier publications;\n          ;; immutable retained content makes that verification reusable.\n          (when (identical? missing (jing/get content-store (:address r) missing))\n            (throw (ex-info \"published content could not be read back\"\n                            {:address (:address r)})))\n          (recur (:state r) (inc n)))\n        :dao.stream/blocked [n nil]\n        [n signal]))))\n\n\n(defn- suffix-state\n  \"Restore verified roots and fold only records after their cursor. The\n   expected record count independently validates the cursor against this\n   composition's one-record-per-transaction log. A stale/foreign cursor,\n   mismatched frontier or rejected record returns nil: the caller must\n   reconstruct in full, never publish an uncertain suffix.\"\n  [ix intake]\n  (let [{:keys [cursor transactions manifest-address manifest max-t]}\n        (:materialization ix)]\n    (when (and manifest-address\n               (= manifest-address (:manifest-address ix))\n               (= transactions (:published ix))\n               (= (:branching-factor manifest)\n                  (:branching-factor (:publish-opts ix) 512)))\n      (try\n        (let [candidate {:manifest-address manifest-address\n                         :mode :resolved :schema-address (jing/segment-key {})\n                         :ids nil :batch transactions :max-t max-t :rejected 0}\n              consumer (index/restore candidate\n                                      {:content-store (:content-store ix)\n                                       :intake intake :mode :resolved :schema {}})\n              expected (- (:transactions ix) transactions)]\n          (loop [cursor cursor, consumer consumer, n 0]\n            (let [r (stream/next (:local ix) cursor)]\n              (when (stream/valid-outcome? :next r)\n                (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n                  :dao.stream/ok\n                  (when (< n expected)\n                    (let [consumer' (index/fold-batch consumer (:dao.stream/value r))]\n                      (when (zero? (:rejected consumer'))\n                        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) consumer' (inc n)))))\n                  (:dao.stream/blocked :dao.stream/end)\n                  (when (= n expected) {:cursor cursor :consumer consumer})\n                  nil)))))\n        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) _\n          nil)))))\n\n\n(defn- enqueue-publication\n  \"Full reconstruction when no validated frontier is available; otherwise\n   publication of the suffix-folded trees through the existing indexer.\"\n  [ix]\n  (let [{:keys [transactor intake]} (:publication ix)]\n    (if-let [{:keys [cursor consumer]} (suffix-state ix intake)]\n      (let [;; A fresh round has exactly one intake; still honor the\n            ;; caller's selection function and its pool-membership rule.\n            select-stream (:select-stream (:publish-opts ix) first)\n            selected (when (fn? select-stream) (select-stream [intake]))\n            _ (when-not (identical? selected intake)\n                (throw (ex-info \"publication must select its round's intake\" {})))\n            {:keys [status state]} (index/publish! consumer)\n            manifest (get-in state [:publish :manifest])]\n        (when-not (= :ok status)\n          (throw (ex-info \"complete-retention publication intake refused\" {:status status})))\n        {:cursor cursor :manifest manifest :manifest-address (jing/segment-key manifest)})\n      (let [result (transactor/publish! transactor (:publish-opts ix))\n            tail (stream/cursor (:local ix) :dao.stream/newest)]\n        (when-not (and (stream/valid-outcome? :cursor tail)\n                       (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome tail)))\n          (throw (ex-info \"published log frontier could not be read\" {:result tail})))\n        (assoc result :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor tail))))))\n\n\n(defn- publish\n  \"Publish the covered indexes over every committed transaction, using\n   the retained frontier when valid, drain the intake, and read the\n   manifest back from it.  Only a publication whose manifest the store\n   answers becomes the reported one, covering `:published` transactions;\n   in durable mode the HEAD pointer moves — `after-publish` — only after\n   that read-back, so a HEAD never names a manifest the store cannot\n   answer, and a HEAD that cannot be written leaves the round reported\n   unpublished.\"\n  [ix round]\n  (try\n    (let [{:keys [pool]} (:publication ix)\n          {:keys [manifest-address manifest cursor]} (enqueue-publication ix)\n          [n defect] (materialize (:content-store ix) pool)]\n      (if defect\n        (assoc ix :failure {:round round :stage :materialize :outcome defect})\n        (do (index/read-manifest (:content-store ix) manifest-address)\n            (when-some [write-head! (:after-publish ix)]\n              (write-head! manifest-address))\n            (cond-> (assoc ix\n                           :manifest-address manifest-address\n                           :published (:transactions ix)\n                           :published-payloads n\n                           :materialization {:cursor cursor\n                                             :transactions (:transactions ix)\n                                             :manifest-address manifest-address\n                                             :manifest manifest\n                                             :max-t (dec (transactor/watermark (:allocator ix)))})\n              (= :publish (:stage (:failure ix))) (assoc :failure nil)))))\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n      (assoc ix\n             :failure {:round round :stage :publish :message (ex-message e)}))))\n\n\n(defn- consume\n(defn step\n  \"The round's index step: observe every packet `program-out` still holds\n   for this observer, commit each through the round's publication, publish\n   when any was committed, then drop the publication's intake, pool and\n   temporary trees. Only the detached allocator and verified covered\n   frontier continue into the next round. A gap is counted on the observer's\n   `:ingress-gaps`, and marks the indexer lost: the missing packet and\n   every later one are never called indexed.\"\n  [indexer round]\n  (let [ix (consume indexer\n                    (fn [ix packet]\n                      (first (commit (open-publication ix) packet round))))\n        committed? (> (:transactions ix) (:transactions indexer))\n        ;; this round's rows and any an earlier round could not write,\n        ;; before any publication: no announcement names a missing row\n        ix (if committed? (write-rows ix round) ix)]\n    (dissoc (if (and committed? (empty? (:unwritten ix)))\n              (publish ix round)\n              ix)\n            :publication)))\n\n\n(defn commit-names\n181:           :value nil)))\n202:           :value nil)))\n490:                      {:type :repl/result :round round :value value}))\n685:   back on the VM as `::result-append`, so a refused append is reported\n692:               ::result-append\n753:   which loads each packet and runs it.  The code indexer's observer\n757:   indexer (`yin.repl.ast-index`), holding the session's `$ast` and `$occ`\n766:   session's `:indexer`, and `:ast-indexer` for `$ast` and `$occ`, as they\n787:     :indexer (index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))\n791:     :ast-indexer (ast-index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))})\n850:   `index-store` is the `dao.jing` byte store the code indexer publishes\n866:   — and the indexer is rehydrated from it here, before any evaluation\n965:               :indexer index/rehydrate (:recovery index-store))\n1100:  (let [append (::result-append vm')\n1104:                        (assoc state' :vm (dissoc vm' ::result-append))))\n1108:      (let [value (:value (peek current))]\n1133:  \"Gaps the evaluation path's observers counted.  The code indexer's are\n1164:                       :indexer (index/skip (:indexer state))\n1165:                       :ast-indexer (ast-index/skip (:ast-indexer state)))\n1175:  \"Drive the code indexer's observer over `program-out`: it commits each\n1180:  (update state :indexer index/step (:round state)))\n1184:  \"Drive the AST indexer's observer over `program-out`: it adds each\n1187:   code indexer does, and neither indexer reads the other.\"\n1189:  (update state :ast-indexer ast-index/step))\n1277:                  ::indexer (:indexer state))))\n1285:   indexer a `yin.link/publish` committed its name envelopes through.\"\n1291:    (::indexer d) (assoc :indexer (::indexer d))))\n1325:   indexer and the VM runs on.  Only a round the VM spends waiting on a\n1362:                                       :indexer (:indexer state)\n1363:                                       :ast-indexer (:ast-indexer state)\n1374:                                      :indexer (:indexer answered)))\n1631:   the expander, drains its summary, and drives the code and AST indexers and then\n1678:                  [(index/notice (:indexer expanded) (:indexer indexed))\n1679:                   (ast-index/notice (:ast-indexer indexed))])))))))))\n1831:   new indexer continues the old one's log, entity allocation, and\n1844:           (update :indexer index/carry-over (:indexer state)))\n2128:(defn eval-input\n2162:(defn repl-state\n2176:   code indexer's `yin.repl.index/status`: whether every committed program\n2177:   is published, whether a gap lost the indexer, and its last failure.\n2178:   `:index-publication` exposes the verified code-log cursor and covered\n2180:   `:ast-index` is the AST indexer's `yin.repl.ast-index/status`: the sizes\n2206:   :index (index/status (:indexer state))\n2207:   :index-publication (select-keys (get-in state [:indexer :materialization])\n2209:   :ast-index (ast-index/status (:ast-indexer state))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj; sed -n '450,565p' src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj; rg --files collab/jolt | rg 'gate2[23]|BRIEF|v3|criterion'; rg -n 'confidence|600|500|10 Hz|outstanding|p99' BRIEF-j6g.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj; sed -n '450,565p' src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj; rg --files collab/jolt | rg 'gate2[23]|BRIEF|v3|criterion'; rg -n 'confidence|600|500|10 Hz|outstanding|p99' BRIEF-j6g.md\"","aggregated_output":"(ns jolt-workload-w-run\n  \"Independent watchdog and sampler for the single-threaded Workload W worker.\n   Run with bb workload-w:jolt [workload-w|quick-w|cross-host|served-stream|all].\"\n  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.string :as str]))\n\n\n(def hard-cap-ms 300000)\n(def telemetry-ms 10000)\n\n\n(defn- now-ms\n  []\n  (quot (System/nanoTime) 1000000))\n\n\n(defn- p99\n  [samples]\n  (when (seq samples)\n    (nth (sort samples) (min (dec (count samples)) (int (* 0.99 (count samples)))))))\n\n\n(defn- observe-line\n  [state line]\n  (if (str/starts-with? line \"W-SAMPLE \")\n    (let [sample (edn/read-string (subs line 9))]\n      (when-not (and (number? sample) (<= 0 sample))\n        (throw (ex-info \"Invalid worker sample\" {:line line})))\n      (-> state\n          (update :samples conj sample)\n          (assoc :last-output-at (now-ms))))\n    (do\n      (println line)\n      (flush)\n      (cond-> (assoc state :last-output-at (now-ms))\n        (str/starts-with? line \"W-PHASE \") (assoc :phase (subs line 8))\n        (= line \"FAIL workload-w\") (assoc :reported-failure? true)))))\n\n\n(defn- read-output\n  \"Only ready characters, at most 8192 per turn: a partial line or a noisy\n   worker must not block the watchdog's clock or its ten-second sampler.\"\n  [reader state]\n  (let [chunk (StringBuilder.)]\n    (loop [remaining 8192]\n      (when (and (pos? remaining) (.ready reader))\n        (let [c (.read reader)]\n          (when (not= -1 c)\n            (.append chunk (char c))\n            (recur (dec remaining))))))\n    (let [lines (str/split (str (:partial state) chunk) #\"\\n\" -1)]\n      (assoc (reduce observe-line state (butlast lines)) :partial (last lines)))))\n\n\n(defn- telemetry!\n  [state elapsed]\n  (println \"WATCHDOG TELEMETRY\"\n           (pr-str {:elapsed-ms elapsed,\n                    :samples (count (:samples state)),\n                    :running-p99-ms (p99 (:samples state)),\n                    :first-round-phase (:phase state),\n                    :output-age-ms (- (now-ms) (:last-output-at state))}))\n  (flush))\n\n\n(defn- failure!\n  [state elapsed reason]\n  (println \"Workload W Results: FAILURE\")\n  (println \"RECORD failure reason\" reason)\n  (println \"RECORD p99 ABSENT\")\n  (println \"RECORD sample count\" (count (:samples state)))\n  (println \"RECORD elapsed ms\" elapsed)\n  (println \"FAIL workload-w\")\n  (flush))\n\n\n(defn- run-watched\n  [args]\n  (let [started (now-ms)\n        command (into [\"sh\" \"-c\"\n                       \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj \\\"$@\\\"\"\n                       \"jolt\"] args)\n        builder (ProcessBuilder. ^java.util.List command)\n        _ (.put (.environment builder) \"JOLT_WORKLOAD_W_SUPERVISED\" \"1\")\n        _ (.redirectError builder java.lang.ProcessBuilder$Redirect/INHERIT)\n        process (.start builder)]\n    (try\n      (with-open [reader (java.io.BufferedReader.\n                          (java.io.InputStreamReader. (.getInputStream process) \"UTF-8\"))]\n        (loop [state {:samples [], :partial \"\", :phase \"loading\", :last-output-at started}\n               next-telemetry (+ started telemetry-ms)]\n          (let [state (read-output reader state)\n                now (now-ms)\n                elapsed (- now started)]\n            (when (>= now next-telemetry)\n              (telemetry! state elapsed))\n            (cond\n              (>= elapsed hard-cap-ms)\n              (do\n                ;; Kill directly: the shell execs jolt, so no worker is left behind.\n                (.destroyForcibly process)\n                (failure! state elapsed :hard-cap)\n                1)\n\n              (not (.isAlive process))\n              ;; Drain already-buffered output without waiting for another line.\n              (if (.ready reader)\n                (recur state next-telemetry)\n                (let [state (if (str/blank? (:partial state))\n                              state\n                              (observe-line state (:partial state)))\n                      status (.exitValue process)]\n                  (when (and (not (zero? status)) (not (:reported-failure? state)))\n                    (failure! state elapsed :worker-failure))\n                  status))\n\n              :else\n              (do\n                (Thread/sleep 10)\n                (recur state (if (>= now next-telemetry)\n                               (+ now telemetry-ms)\n                               next-telemetry)))))))\n      (finally\n        (when (.isAlive process) (.destroyForcibly process))))))\n\n\n(System/exit (run-watched *command-line-args*))\n\n                  ;; 5. Pump I/O for server and client B\n                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n                    (println \"W-PHASE server-pump\")\n                    (flush))\n                  (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 server-pump nil)\n                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n                    (println \"W-PHASE client-b-pump\")\n                    (flush))\n                  (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 client-b-pump nil)\n                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n                    (println \"W-PHASE owner-round-complete\")\n                    (flush))\n\n                  ;; Check exit conditions\n                  (let [a-done? (or @a-stalled?\n                                    (and (>= @a-sent total-a-frame-len)\n                                         (seq @a-deliveries)))\n                        time-done? (>= elapsed target-duration-ms)\n                        samples-done? (>= (count @b-samples) target-samples)]\n\n                    (if (and a-done? time-done? samples-done?)\n                      ;; Drain trailing in-flight requests briefly\n                      (let [drain-deadline (+ (poller/clock-ms) 500)]\n                        (loop []\n                          (when (and (seq @b-outstanding)\n                                     (< (poller/clock-ms) (min deadline drain-deadline)))\n                            (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 server-pump nil)\n                            (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 client-b-pump nil)\n                            (recur))))\n                      (recur)))))))\n\n          ;; Cleanup sockets\n          (raw-close! raw-a)\n          (wsj/close-host! client-b-inst)\n          (wsj/close-host! server-inst)\n          (wake/close! w)\n\n          ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------\n          ;; Evaluation of pre-registered criterion\n          ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------\n          (let [sample-count (count @b-samples)\n                elapsed-ms (- (poller/clock-ms) run-start)\n                valid-run? (>= sample-count 500)\n                target-samples-met? (>= sample-count target-samples)\n                sorted (sort @b-samples)\n                p99-idx (int (* 0.99 sample-count))\n                p99 (when (and (not @timed-out?) (pos? sample-count))\n                      (nth sorted (min (dec sample-count) p99-idx)))\n                p99-ok? (and (some? p99) (<= p99 250))\n                repl-advances? (= @owner-round-count @repl-step-count)\n                a-deliv-count (count @a-deliveries)\n                a-deliv-len (or (first @a-deliveries) 0)\n                delivered-once? (and (= 1 a-deliv-count)\n                                     (= 4194304 a-deliv-len))\n                replies-lost (count @b-outstanding)\n                no-reply-lost? (and (zero? @b-lost) (zero? replies-lost))\n                all-pass? (and (not @timed-out?)\n                               (not @a-stalled?)\n                               valid-run?\n                               target-samples-met?\n                               p99-ok?\n                               repl-advances?\n                               delivered-once?\n                               no-reply-lost?)]\n\n            (println)\n            (println \"================================================================================\")\n            (println \"Workload W Results:\" (if all-pass? \"SUCCESS\" \"FAILURE\"))\n            (println \"================================================================================\")\n            (println \"  Hard cap timed out:           \" @timed-out?)\n            (println \"  Elapsed:                      \" elapsed-ms \"ms\")\n            (println \"  Peer A transfer stalled:      \" @a-stalled?)\n            (println \"  Sample count:                 \" sample-count\n                     (str \"(valid >= 500: \" valid-run? \", target >= \" target-samples \": \" target-samples-met? \")\"))\n            (println \"  p99 round-trip latency:       \" (if (some? p99) (str p99 \"ms\") \"ABSENT\")\n                     (str \"(criterion <= 250 ms: \" p99-ok? \")\"))\n            (println \"  Peer B replies lost:          \" replies-lost \"(unanswered) +\" @b-lost \"(corrupt)\")\n            (println \"  Peer A delivered once:        \" delivered-once?\n                     (str \"(deliveries: \" a-deliv-count \", bytes: \" a-deliv-len \", sent: \" @a-sent \")\"))\n            (println \"  REPL per-round step advance:  \" repl-advances?\n                     (str \"(rounds: \" @owner-round-count \", REPL steps: \" @repl-step-count \")\"))\n            (println)\n\n            ;; Required report records per BRIEF-j6g.md\n            (if (some? p99)\n              (println \"RECORD p99\" p99 \"ms\")\n              (println \"RECORD p99 ABSENT\"))\n            (println \"RECORD sample count\" sample-count)\n            (println \"RECORD elapsed ms\" elapsed-ms)\n            (println \"RECORD delivered once\" delivered-once?)\n            (println \"RECORD per-round step advance\" repl-advances?)\n\n            (if all-pass?\n              (do (println \"PASS workload-w\")\n                  {:pass? true\n                   :p99 p99\n                   :samples sample-count\n                   :elapsed-ms elapsed-ms\n                   :timed-out? @timed-out?\n                   :transfer-stalled? @a-stalled?\n                   :delivered-once? delivered-once?\n                   :repl-advances? repl-advances?\n                   :replies-lost replies-lost})\n              (do (println \"FAIL workload-w\")\n                  {:pass? false\n                   :p99 p99\n                   :samples sample-count\n                   :elapsed-ms elapsed-ms\n                   :timed-out? @timed-out?\n                   :transfer-stalled? @a-stalled?\n                   :delivered-once? delivered-once?\n                   :repl-advances? repl-advances?\n                   :replies-lost replies-lost}))))))))\n\n\nrg: BRIEF-j6g.md: IO error for operation on BRIEF-j6g.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"The local harness differs from the reported instrumented run: it discards result entries and counts calls as REPL steps. I’m tracing the frontend state wrapper and publication path to determine what the reported zero results and nil cursor actually establish."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc; sed -n '1050,1135p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '1615,1685p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '2110,2220p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '1,70p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '460,505p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc; sed -n '1050,1135p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '1615,1685p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '2110,2220p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '1,70p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '460,505p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.repl.frontends\n  \"The REPL's standard frontend catalog (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section\n   8.5.6, slice F2): the hand-written Clojure and PHP frontends and the\n   ANTLR Python frontend installed into a `yang.frontend` catalog. This is\n   the only place the REPL composition names a language's namespace;\n   `yin.repl` core steps whatever binding the catalog selects.\n\n   A binding is `{:parse (fn [input]) :lower (fn [parsed])}`, with\n   `:input :forms` when the frontend consumes the forms the shell reader\n   already read, else the source text.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\n    [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n    [yang.php :as yang.php]\n    #?@(:cljd [[yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.antlr.repl]\n               [yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\n               [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.antlr.probe]]\n        :default [[yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.antlr.repl]\n                  [yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\n                  [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.antlr.probe]])\n    [yin.repl :as repl]))\n\n\n(defn- manifest\n  [id language]\n  {:yang.frontend/id id,\n   :yang.frontend/spi 1,\n   :yang.frontend/revision \"legacy-1\",\n   :yang.frontend/language language,\n   :yang.frontend/grammar {:yang.grammar/package \"none\",\n                           :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"program\"},\n                           :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1},\n   :yang.frontend/options-schema :segment/none,\n   :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :segment/legacy,\n   :yang.frontend/runtime-profile :segment/legacy,\n   :yang.frontend/support-profile :segment/legacy})\n\n\n(defn- clojure-lower\n  [forms]\n  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n\n\n(defn- antlr-manifest\n  []\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/python :python)\n         :yang.frontend/revision \"f4\"\n         :yang.frontend/grammar\n         {:yang.grammar/package \"python3\",\n          :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"file_input\"},\n          :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1,\n          :yang.grammar/targets #{:java :javascript :dart}}))\n\n\n(defn standard\n  \"The standard catalog. The Clojure frontend consumes the forms the\n   shell's own reader read, so its parse stage is the identity.  The ANTLR\n   frontend is the Python frontend, installed on every host, each running\n   its own generated target of the one grammar.  It shows what a submission\n   printed and the value rendered by its `:render` (Python repr).\"\n  []\n  (cond-> frontend/empty-catalog\n    true (frontend/install (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n                           {:input :forms,\n                            :parse identity,\n                            :lower clojure-lower})\n    true (frontend/install (manifest :yang/php :php)\n                           {:parse identity, :lower yang.php/compile})\n    #?@(:cljd [true (frontend/install\n                      (antlr-manifest)\n                      {:parse (fn [source]\n                                (python.antlr.parser/parse-source (str source \"\\n\"))),\n                       :lower python.antlr.repl/lower,\n                       :primitives python.antlr.repl/primitives,\n                       :lower-session python.antlr.repl/lower-session,\n                       :render python.antlr.repl/display-value,\n                       :probe python.antlr.probe/probe})]\n        ;; jolt (J5): installed over the C++ parser when native/jolt-parser\n        ;; is available; otherwise left out, so (lang :yang/python) answers\n        ;; unavailable-parser, never another parser\n        :jolt [(python.antlr.parser/available?)\n               (frontend/install\n                 (antlr-manifest)\n                 {;; a :parser-budget or :unavailable-parser refusal names\n                  ;; the language it refused\n                  :parse (fn [source]\n                           (try (python.antlr.parser/parse-source (str source \"\\n\"))\n                                (catch Exception e\n                                  (if (#{:parser-budget :unavailable-parser}\n                                       (:diagnostic (ex-data e)))\n                                    (throw (ex-info (ex-message e)\n                                                    (assoc (ex-data e) :lang :yang/python)\n                                                    e))\n                                    (throw e))))),\n                  :lower python.antlr.repl/lower,\n                  :primitives python.antlr.repl/primitives,\n                  :lower-session python.antlr.repl/lower-session,\n                  :render python.antlr.repl/display-value,\n                  :probe python.antlr.probe/probe})]\n        :default [true (frontend/install\n                         (antlr-manifest)\n                         {:parse (fn [source]\n                                   (python.antlr.parser/parse-source (str source \"\\n\"))),\n                          :lower python.antlr.repl/lower,\n                          :primitives python.antlr.repl/primitives,\n                          :lower-session python.antlr.repl/lower-session,\n                          :render python.antlr.repl/display-value,\n                          :probe python.antlr.probe/probe})])))\n\n\n(defn create-state\n  \"`yin.repl/create-state` composed with the standard catalog unless the\n   host supplies its own `:frontends`.  Each binding registers its own\n   `:primitives`; none is merged ambiently.\"\n  ([] (create-state {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (repl/create-state (update opts :frontends #(or % (standard))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Evaluation\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- inject-last-value\n  [state]\n  (update state :vm update :store assoc\n          '*1 (:last-value state)\n          '*2 (:last-value-2 state)\n          '*3 (:last-value-3 state)))\n\n\n(defn- record-last-value\n  [state state-after value]\n  (assoc state-after\n         :last-value value\n         :last-value-2 (:last-value state)\n         :last-value-3 (:last-value-2 state)))\n\n\n(defn- round-id\n  \"The identity of the state's current round: the shell's token, minted\n   once per shell value, with its round count.  A medium the caller\n   supplies may already hold results from another shell or an earlier\n   round; none of them carries this identity.\"\n  [state]\n  [(:shell-token state) (:round state)])\n\n\n(defn- commit-frontend\n  \"Keep what a frontend program's lowering staged (`::frontend`, see\n   `eval-compiled`) now that its VM state survives: the frontend session\n   it leaves becomes the shell's `:frontend-session`.\"\n  [state]\n  (let [staged (::frontend state)]\n    (cond-> (dissoc state ::frontend)\n      (contains? staged :session) (assoc :frontend-session (:session staged)))))\n\n\n(defn- finalize-eval\n  \"Drain the round's output and its result from the output medium.  Only a\n   result stamped with this round's identity is this round's value; the\n   evaluator answers once per halted program, after its prints.  A missing\n   or foreign-round result is loss, reported with the append outcome the\n   runner recorded.  The program halted, so its VM state survives and a\n   frontend's staged session is committed; a frontend with a `:render`\n   shows its value as that renders it, the loop printing for every language.\"\n  [state state' vm']\n  (let [append (::result-append vm')\n        render (:render (::frontend state'))\n        [state'' output-text results]\n        (drain-output (commit-frontend\n                        (assoc state' :vm (dissoc vm' ::result-append))))\n        round (round-id state')\n        current (filterv #(= round (:round %)) results)]\n    (if (seq current)\n      (let [value (:value (peek current))]\n        [(record-last-value state state'' value)\n         (str output-text\n              (if render\n                (render value)\n                (format-value value (host-fn-namer (:vm state'')))))])\n      [state''\n       (str output-text \"Error: \" result-loss-text\n            (when (and append (not= :dao.stream/ok append))\n              (str \" (append: \" (name append) \")\")))])))\n\n\n(defn- drain-observer\n  \"Advance one observer past every batch still on its medium, keeping any\n   gap it recovers across.  A nil observer — a session without that medium —\n   stays nil.\"\n  [observer]\n  (when observer\n    (loop [observer observer]\n      (let [{:keys [status] observer' :observer}\n            (observer/observe-next observer)]\n        (if (#{:ok :gap} status) (recur observer') observer')))))\n\n\n(defn- ingress-gaps\n  \"Gaps the evaluation path's observers counted.  The code indexer's are\n   its own: an index loss is reported without refusing evaluation.\"\n  [state]\n                   (if (or (::link-counter d) (::link-origins d))\n                     (carry-link-identity\n                       (:vm state)\n                       {:id-counter (::link-counter d)\n                        :origins (::link-origins d)})\n                     (:vm state))\n                   (:query-pair expanded))]\n        (consume-failed-round (carry-served (assoc expanded :vm base) d)\n                              error)))))\n\n\n(defn- eval-program\n  \"Evaluate one frontend program — the map AST the compilers emit or a\n   datom-literal program — through the §10.1 composition.  The encoder\n   projects it to an input batch of canonical rows with its harvest and\n   declaration rows; the shell appends that batch to `program-in`, drives\n   the expander, drains its summary, and drives the code and AST indexers and then\n   the evaluator only when a program was forwarded.  An expansion failure is reported as data: its\n   batch is consumed, the store keeps its previous macros, and the next\n   input evaluates normally.  An encoding failure throws before anything\n   is appended.\n\n   The observers recover across a gap on their own, but the shell reads the\n   gap counts around the round: an increase on any medium means one or more\n   batches were never run, so resuming as though execution were complete\n   would report a result built on programs the VM never saw.  The loss is\n   reported and the shell refuses further evaluation until `(reset)`.\n\n   A completed program's lexical environment does not outlive it: the VM's\n   environment is restored to the one the round began with, as `vm/eval`\n   does.  A round that throws is consumed by `consume-failed-round`.\"\n  [state program]\n  (if (:ingress-loss? state)\n    [state (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n    (let [state' (update (inject-last-value state) :round inc)\n          batch (encoder/program-batch program)\n          append (stream/append! (:program-stream state') batch)]\n      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome append))\n        [state (str \"Error: program batch not ingested: \"\n                    (name (:dao.stream/outcome append)))]\n        (let [expanded (try\n                         (run-expander-stage state')\n                         (catch #?(:cljd Object\n                                   :clj Exception\n                                   :cljs js/Error) error\n                           {:failed (consume-failed-round state error)}))]\n          (if-let [failed (:failed expanded)]\n            failed\n            (let [[expanded {:keys [errors forwarded]}] expanded\n                  indexed (cond-> expanded\n                            (pos? forwarded) (-> run-index-stage\n                                                 run-ast-index-stage))]\n              (with-index-notice\n                (cond\n                  (> (ingress-gaps indexed) (ingress-gaps state'))\n                  [(assoc indexed :ingress-loss? true)\n                   (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n\n                  (pos? forwarded) (run-evaluation state indexed)\n\n                  :else [(assoc indexed :vm (:vm state))\n                         (format-expansion-errors errors)])\n                (when (pos? forwarded)\n                  [(index/notice (:indexer expanded) (:indexer indexed))\n                   (ast-index/notice (:ast-indexer indexed))])))))))))\n\n\n(defn- installed-text\n  \"The languages and ids `catalog` holds, for a refused selection to name:\n   a name that is neither is a typo, not a missing frontend.\"\n  [catalog]\n(defn- eval-parsed\n  [state trimmed parsed]\n  (if (and (:pending-run state) (not (command-line? parsed)))\n    ;; A require is still pending: re-check it first.  While it stays\n    ;; pending the line is retained -- the parked VM owns the store a new\n    ;; evaluation would fork -- and it evaluates, in typing order and\n    ;; exactly once, when the link completes.\n    (resume-pending state trimmed parsed)\n    (eval-parsed* state trimmed parsed)))\n\n\n(defn- input-probe\n  \"The completeness probe of the session's frontend, or nil when it has\n   none or none is installed (the compile then reports it).\"\n  [state]\n  (:probe (usable-binding (select-frontend (:frontends state) (:lang state)))))\n\n\n(defn eval-input\n  \"Evaluate one input line locally, returning `[state text]`.\n\n   Input that is not yet a whole submission is retained as `:pending-input`\n   and produces no text: for a frontend with a `:probe` the probe decides\n   and the line is kept verbatim (whitespace can be inside a string);\n   otherwise the brackets must balance.  Nothing here is asynchronous: the\n   driver, not this namespace, decides when the next step happens.\"\n  [state line]\n  (let [probe (input-probe state)\n        pending (or (:pending-input state) \"\")\n        line (if probe line (str/trim line))\n        combined (if (str/blank? pending)\n                   line\n                   (str pending \"\\n\" line))]\n    (cond\n      (and probe (str/blank? combined))\n      [(assoc state :pending-input nil) \"\"]\n\n      (if probe\n        (= :incomplete (probe combined))\n        (pos? (bracket-balance combined)))\n      [(assoc state :pending-input combined) \"\"]\n\n      :else\n      (let [state' (assoc state :pending-input nil)\n            parsed (try {:forms (read-forms combined)}\n                        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n                                  :clj Exception\n                                  :cljs js/Error) error\n                          {:error error}))]\n        (eval-parsed state' combined parsed)))))\n\n\n(defn repl-state\n  \"A serializable summary of shell state.\n\n   The stream summaries read the ledger rather than asking a handle whether it\n   is closed: dao.stream has no `closed?`, and an idle medium has no last\n   operation.\n   The program media are the composition's own, observed beside the VM, so\n   the shell reports what it knows of them — the declared capacity, the gaps\n   the session's observers counted, and whether a loss has already refused\n   further evaluation.  Each `:pending` entry carries the link policy's\n   name (`:manual` or `:fn`) and the pending run's `:checks`, so a host\n   can display why a run is still waiting (yin.repl.link-policy.md\n   section 3.5).  `:macros` maps each macro the expander's store holds\n   to its lambda's root address (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1).  `:index` is the\n   code indexer's `yin.repl.index/status`: whether every committed program\n   is published, whether a gap lost the indexer, and its last failure.\n   `:index-publication` exposes the verified code-log cursor and covered\n   transaction count for owner diagnostics, never a substitute query view.\n   `:ast-index` is the AST indexer's `yin.repl.ast-index/status`: the sizes\n   of its `$ast` and `$occ` relations, whether a gap lost it, and why it\n   failed.\"\n  [state]\n  {:lang (:lang state)\n   :macros (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (str %1) (str %2)))\n                 (map (fn [[sym entry]]\n                        [sym (first (:yin.macro/tree entry))]))\n                 (get-in state [:expander :ctx :store]))\n   :vm {:type (:vm-type state)\n        :halted? (vm/halted? (:vm state))\n        :blocked? (vm/blocked? (:vm state))\n        :in-stream {:capacity ingress-capacity\n                    :gaps (ingress-gaps state)\n                    :lost? (boolean (:ingress-loss? state))}}\n   :running? (:running? state)\n   :output {:cursor (:output-cursor state)\n            :last-outcome (get-in state [:ledger :output] :untried)}\n   :pending (when-let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n              (let [policy (:link-policy state)]\n                (mapv (fn [p]\n                        {:name (:name p)\n                         :link-id (:yin.link/id p)\n                         :policy (if (fn? policy) :fn policy)\n                         :checks (or (:checks parked) 0)})\n                      (:links parked))))\n   :index (index/status (:indexer state))\n   :index-publication (select-keys (get-in state [:indexer :materialization])\n                                   [:cursor :transactions :manifest-address])\n   :ast-index (ast-index/status (:ast-indexer state))\n   :telemetry {:supported? false :note telemetry-text}\n   :remote {:connected? false}})\n(ns yin.repl.driver\n  \"The one owner of Yin REPL state.\n\n   A line producer appends `{:yin.repl.input/line \\\"…\\\"}` to the\n   composition-owned input medium and returns.  It does not evaluate, request,\n   poll, print, prompt, or touch the state held here.  `repl-step` is called\n   once per externally driven tick by exactly one ticker per host: it drains\n   the input medium, evaluates local input, forwards ordinary source through\n   the RPC client, publishes completions exactly once, and returns the next\n   state.\n\n   It never loops on `blocked`, and it owns no promise, future, callback, atom,\n   or clock.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.data :as data]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]\n            [yin.repl.adapter :as adapter]\n            [yin.repl.connect :as connect]\n            [yin.repl :as repl]\n            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]\n            [yin.repl.host :as host]))\n\n\n(def line-key :yin.repl.input/line)\n\n\n(def input-capacity\n  \"Declared capacity of the composition-owned input medium, in elements.\"\n  1024)\n\n\n(def input-budget\n  \"Maximum input elements one step reads, so a flooded medium cannot make a\n   single step unbounded.\"\n  64)\n\n\n(def response-budget\n  \"Maximum response-medium elements one step reads.\"\n  32)\n\n\n(def event-key :yin.repl.driver/event)\n(def text-key :yin.repl.driver/text)\n\n\n(def ^:private diagnostic-bounds\n  \"Bound on operator-facing diagnostic text built from unbounded internal\n   state (raw input, event/result maps).\"\n  {:depth 3 :items 8 :chars 200})\n\n\n(def connect-usage\n  (str \"(connect \\\"daostream:ws://host:port/repl\\\" [:codec :cbor|:transit]) \"\n       \"— an absent path means /repl, an absent codec means :cbor\"))\n\n\n(defn create-input-medium!\n  \"Create the composition-owned input ring buffer.  The handoff between a line\n   producer and the step owner is a stream, which is what makes it explicit and\n   thread-safe.\"\n  []\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n                   ring/capacity-key input-capacity})))\n\n\n(defn- mint-cursor\n\n(defn- prn-text\n  [args]\n  (str (str/join \" \" (map format-value args)) \"\\n\"))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The output medium\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- emit-output!\n  [output-stream op text]\n  ;; A primitive holds no state, so it cannot record an append outcome.  The\n  ;; medium is an evict-oldest ring buffer, which never answers `full`; a closed\n  ;; medium drops the chunk and the drain reports the closure.\n  (when output-stream\n    (stream/append! output-stream {:type :repl/output :op op :text text}))\n  nil)\n\n\n(defn- emit-result!\n  \"Answer a halted evaluation's value on the output medium, after the\n   output it printed, so the shell reads results from the stream exactly as\n   it reads prints.  The token carries `round`, so the shell accepts only\n   this round's result.  Returns the append outcome, or `:untried` when\n   there is no medium.\"\n  [output-stream round value]\n  (if output-stream\n    (:dao.stream/outcome\n      (stream/append! output-stream\n                      {:type :repl/result :round round :value value}))\n    :untried))\n\n\n(defn- make-repl-primitives\n  [output-stream]\n  (merge vm/primitives\n         {'print (fn [& args]\n                   (emit-output! output-stream :print (print-text args)))\n          'println (fn [& args]\n                     (emit-output! output-stream :println\n                                   (str (print-text args) \"\\n\")))\n          'prn (fn [& args] (emit-output! output-stream :prn (prn-text args)))\n          'ast->datoms vm/ast->datoms\n          'datoms->ast vm/datoms->ast}))\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
