ception reasons then cite that row. Pinning 7.9.x to 1002 as well is optional.\ncollab/jolt/1794006000000-architect-j6g-ruling.gpt-6.1-sol.ruling.md:7:**Disposition:** J6g remains **FAILED**: 79 samples is below 600, and p99 ≈7.9 s exceeds 250 ms. Delivered-once and REPL advancement satisfy only their respective legs. The criterion stands. No code changes or remote runs were performed in this ruling round.\ncollab/jolt/1794006000000-architect-j6g-ruling.gpt-6.1-sol.ruling.md:89:- At least **600** qualifying overlapping B round trips complete, with **p99 ≤250 ms** and no lost reply.\ncollab/jolt/1794006000000-architect-j6g-ruling.gpt-6.1-sol.ruling.md:93:Post-transfer replies cannot fill the sample target. The 500-sample validity floor is not a pass threshold. A watchdog timeout, incomplete evidence, or any unmet leg leaves J6g unpassed. The five-minute cap is a safety limit, not a replacement transfer window.\ncollab/jolt/1793140000000-architect-j4d-cosign.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md:10:Perform a READ-ONLY review of branch origin/jolt-j4d (tip f35df68a, six commits on merge-base 671cd21f) against docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md (§5 Files/Store/Signing/Main rows, §10.1 J4 row) and the J4d acceptance: the file: store opens on jolt (only dht: refuses, at composition); saved flags persist through the jolt -main (--reset, --no-state); key files are created O_CREAT|O_EXCL at 0600 and never overwritten; no J4-owned entry remains in jolt-applicability.edn or the J2 lane; failure semantics of native/jolt-file layout 3.\ncollab/jolt/1792560133000-reviewer-jolt-j1-r3.glm-5.3.prompt.md:10:Your round 1-2 review: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792557634000-reviewer-jolt-j1.glm-5.3.findings.md . Round 3 is UNCOMMITTED in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j1 on top of commit f6f3ca00 (git diff there: src/dev/jolt_json_test.cljc, src/dev/jolt_profile_compare.cljc, src/jolt/clojure/data/json.jolt, src/jolt/dao/host/text.jolt). Report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792559718000-engineer-jolt-j1-r3.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md . The orchestrator re-ran: smoke rc 0, runner self-test rc 0, json 8 tests/57 assertions rc 0, test:jolt-host unchanged (bytes 98/98 + 3 load failures on boring/core), diag unchanged, compare 1596 cases and 44 differences (88 differing lines). Check: (1) J1-R5: units->string above 0xFFFF now throws exactly the JVM's IllegalArgumentException \"Value out of range for char: u\" with no ex-data, first such unit in order, before any surrogate handling: confirm against the shared src/cljc/dao/host/text.cljc and the JVM behaviour, and that the surrogate :jolt/unimplemented seam is untouched; (2) J1-R3: the json shim header annotation and the pinned test rows: is the claim \"keywords are written by name on the JVM too (data.json 2.5.0), only DEL differs\" right (check the shim and, if you can, data.json's source in the repo's dependency cache under ~/.m2 is outside the allowed read root so say so if unverifiable); (3) J1-R4: the 56 new compare cases for dao.host.number float64-of/float-value on decimal and ratio carriers: decimals identical in 32 cases; 3 of 12 ratio inputs differ (6 cases): the author claims the JVM is wrong (Clojure's Ratio.doubleValue rounds twice: first to 16 decimal digits, then to a double; e.g. (2^53+3)/2^53 is an exact tie that must round to even 3ff0000000000002 but the JVM gives 1.0 = 3ff0000000000000, and 2/3 should be 3fe5555555555555 but the JVM gives ...556) and that the profile's own shared kernel dao.host.float/ratio->float agrees with jolt when run on the JVM: verify by reading src/cljc/dao/host/float.cljc and src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc (which entry does the JVM arm of number use for a ratio?), and judge whether the author was right NOT to change jolt and to mark them a known difference; is the claim of a JVM defect in the SHARED code credible, and which file/line would carry the fix (that goes to the host-boundary seat as a defect report); (4) the remaining compare differences (44): carrier type 31, big-carrier? 1, surrogate 5, ->Rational arglists metadata 1, JVM ratio rounding 6: is each class acceptable and correctly labelled; (5) scope (nothing under src/cljc, test/dao/host, docs/design touched); the report's honesty. Write ONLY /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560133000-reviewer-jolt-j1-r3.glm-5.3.findings.md (header fields; verdict SIGNED OFF / SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES / NOT SIGNED OFF; findings table id, severity, file:line, evidence, correction; what you could not verify; under 600 words) and end your final response with its path. Read only under /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld. Do not enter plan mode.\ncollab/jolt/1792430106000-reviewer-jolt-j0b-udp-probe-r2.glm-5.3.prompt.md:10:The author fixed your findings. Read the corrected report /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792429967000-engineer-jolt-j0b-udp-probe-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md, the modified /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/build/jolt-spike/j0b/udp_probe.clj and run.sh, and run-4..6.log. The orchestrator re-ran: 36 assertions pass, 0 fail, 3 records. Confirm for each of your R1-R6 (and the informational notes) CLOSED / NOT CLOSED / PARTIAL with file:line evidence; check that every number in the new report now appears in run-4..6.log; check the author's claim that MSG_TRUNC is at socket.h:574 (not your :576) against the local SDK headers and say who was right; check that no new assertion is a tautology. Under 350 words. Write ONLY /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792430106000-reviewer-jolt-j0b-udp-probe-r2.glm-5.3.findings.md (same header fields) with a verdict SIGNED OFF / NOT SIGNED OFF. Do not enter plan mode.\ncollab/jolt/1793140000000-architect-j4d-cosign.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:18:- **Key security:** creation uses `O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_CLOEXEC` with mode `0600`; umask can only restrict it further. Writes use the acquired descriptor, avoiding a create/reopen race. Existing final-path symlinks cannot be followed by this exclusive create. Seeds stay out of the inspected diagnostics and subprocess arguments. [jolt_file.c:366](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/native/jolt-file/jolt_file.c:366), [file.jolt:620](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/jolt/dao/posix/file.jolt:620)\ncollab/jolt/1793072368523-architect-j4d-review.moonshot-kimi-k3.1-pro.prompt.md:14:  O_CREAT | O_EXCL | O_CLOEXEC, 0600) and jolt_file_eexist; 24 exports,\ncollab/jolt/1793072368523-architect-j4d-review.moonshot-kimi-k3.1-pro.prompt.md:36:- The J4b review's F8 and the spec §5 Signing/Main rows (0600 key files;\ncollab/jolt/1793072368523-architect-j4d-review.moonshot-kimi-k3.1-pro.prompt.md:48:2. THE KEY FILES: 0600 from creation (O_EXCL, never overwrite, EEXIST\ncollab/jolt/1792491122000-reviewer-jolt-j0c-r2.qwen3.8-max.prompt.md:10:READ-ONLY review of the UNCOMMITTED round-2 change in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c (branch jolt-j0c, HEAD fd0adf80): modified native/jolt-parser/jolt_parser.cpp, src/jolt/README.md; new src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt, src/dev/jolt_j0c_oracle.clj, src/dev/jolt_j0c_parity.clj, src/dev/jolt-j0c-probe-stub/yang/python/antlr/parser.clj, test/yang/python/antlr/fixtures/jolt_j0c_corpus.edn and jolt_j0c_oracle.edn. Report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md; spec: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md sections 7.3 to 7.8. The orchestrator re-ran: oracle regenerates (51 entries, 40 probe texts), native rebuild exit 0, parity run \"5 diverged, 0 failed\", all 51 completeness results and 40 probe answers match. The standard for the 5 syntax-error divergences is being ruled by the Architect separately: DO NOT review that question; review correctness and honesty of the work.\ncollab/jolt/1792491122000-reviewer-jolt-j0c-r2.qwen3.8-max.prompt.md:11:Check: (a) ORACLE INTEGRITY: is the oracle generated only from the repo's existing JVM path, never from jolt output; is the order of events (oracle digest recorded before the first jolt run) credible; could the corpus have been tuned to pass; is the corpus faithful to design 7.8 (arithmetic, nested indent/dedent, empty/EOF, non-ASCII and astral, malformed, incomplete multiline, triple quotes, open brackets, early error under an open bracket) and does it avoid ints beyond 64 bits and floats (W8); (b) the new native entry jolt_parser_export and cst.jolt: exception containment preserved (nonallocating failure paths, fault-injection tests still green), buffer ownership, validation of the native buffer before the shared exporter sees it, a failed parse throws and never yields a packet, no pointer or C++ object visible to guest code; (c) the first-failure rule: the author says the C++ token buffer fills lazily like Java's so the adapter uses the JVM rule, and that the JS/Dart rule would be wrong for \"f(1,\\n\": is that evidence solid; (d) the probe stand-in (src/dev/jolt-j0c-probe-stub/...parser.clj): does it make the probe run through the real shared code or could it hide a gap; (e) the experiment that temporarily patched the generated C++ helper: was it fully reverted (digests, byte-identical library claim; verify the manifest digests and the generated files against the recorded ones); (f) is the report honest about what is NOT done. Under 600 words, final response only, header fields, verdict SIGNED OFF / SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES / NOT SIGNED OFF, findings table (id, severity, file:line, evidence, correction), what you could not verify.\ncollab/jolt/1792460482000-reviewer-jolt-j0c-r1-fix.qwen3.8-max.prompt.md:10:You signed off J0c round 1 WITH CHANGES (F1 required, F3 note). The author's fix report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792460256000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r1-fix.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md; worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c (changed: native/jolt-parser/jolt_parser.cpp, src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj, antlr/python3/manifest.edn). The orchestrator re-ran: probe exit 0, 11 PASS (7 original + 4 fault-injection), bb smoke:jolt exit 0.\ncollab/jolt/1793199000001-engineer-j5b-round2-resume.prompt.md:10:Resume J5b round 2 in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-j5b: continue and complete collab/1793196000000-engineer-j5b-round2.prompt.md (in this worktree) with the Architect's binding rulings in collab/fable-j5b-rulings.md. Your log was empty: check git status and the tree to see which of A1, the reclassified legs, the doc/ledger edits D1-D9 you already made (18 files changed), do not redo finished work, finish the rest, run the macOS legs one lane at a time in the foreground, and end with the report the original brief asks for (changed files, per-C-item met/unmet/not run, the Linux commands for the orchestrator, the placeholder line in section 7.6 Platforms). Constraints unchanged (no stage/commit, no collab/ cites in docs or ledger, no bb test:jolt-j5 on the laptop). Begin with Completed-GMT / Completed-Local / Coding-Agent / Session-ID lines.\ncollab/jolt/1792427226000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r7.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:314:| F2 | Accepted | §§1, 7, J5, Q3: JVM/Node/Dart AOT worker parameter; generated-target evidence `yang.antlr.md:496–500,3229–3231`, builds `bb.edn:6–31`. |\ncollab/jolt/1792500314000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r4.claude-opus-5-5.prompt.md:17:Keep green: bb smoke:jolt, the round-1 probe (11 PASS), and the E1 parity harness (SUMMARY ok, E1 51/51). Report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792500314000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r4.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md (header fields; ladder table A-E: DONE / PARTIAL / STOPPED-AT with evidence; the measured budgets and observations; commands/exits; files changed). End with its path.\ncollab/jolt/1792424621000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r4.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:160:- **(a) Generated ANTLR parsing worker — recommended lower-cost completion path; host is a J5 parameter.** `yang.antlr.md:472–509` already specifies local-or-service parsing through streams. V: `yang.antlr.md:496–500,3229–3231` covers generated Python parsers for JVM, Node and Dart. `bb.edn:6–31` builds the Node bundle and Dart AOT peer; these prove available host targets, not an already implemented parsing-worker command. Qualify JVM / Node / Dart AOT over the same stream contract, defaulting to the target already a prerequisite of the lane being run. Among these three worker choices, Dart AOT permits a JVM-free, Node-free deployed parser process tree; the fourth, in-process C++ FFI option below also does so (generation/build prerequisites remain separate). Use the pinned generated parser for that target and export the same sealed CST packets/diagnostics via the existing `yang.stage`/packet contracts. Keep scope/lowering/prelude/primitives/render/session evaluation in jolt. Also route the parser-dependent completeness probe through this worker or its equivalent diagnostic packet; otherwise multiline behavior diverges. One long-lived worker amortizes startup; no process per expression.\ncollab/jolt/1792424621000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r4.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:277:| F2 | Accepted | §§1, 7, J5, Q3: JVM/Node/Dart AOT worker parameter; generated-target evidence `yang.antlr.md:496–500,3229–3231`, builds `bb.edn:6–31`. |\ncollab/jolt/1792500314000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r4.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:123:- Native-only runs (`native` mode) crash at the same depths as full runs (parens: main passes 8,000 and dies before 16,000 in both modes; a jolt thread passes 500 and dies before 1,000), so **the overflow is the native recursion** (ANTLR's recursive descent and the wrapper's walk), not the jolt side.\ncollab/jolt/1792500314000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r4.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:245:Long runs: the tool moves any foreground command past 600 s to the background and stops it 10 minutes later. My first full stack run (part 1: parens, list, call), a `unary not` batch and two sanitize runs were stopped that way. The final full stack run and the 50-cycle sanitize run were then launched with `run_in_background` and a long timeout, and I waited for their completion notifications. No other command ran in the background.\ncollab/jolt/1792500314000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r4.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:255:| `jolt … src/dev/jolt_j0c_cycles.clj 5000` and `… 20000` | 0, 0 | `r4-cycles.log`, `r4-cycles-20000.log` |\ncollab/jolt/1792500314000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r4.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:289:Report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792500314000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r4.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.findings.md:72:server cannot receive, B's producer cannot dispatch at 10 Hz, B's client\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.findings.md:105:very few requests at all. Likewise `p99 ABSENT` is the watchdog's deliberate\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.findings.md:137:  count look sufficient (line 548). The 500 validity floor, 600 default target,\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.findings.md:213:short rounds and a transfer interval admitting 600 exchanges, its numbers are\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.findings.md:215:for those rounds; a larger timeout cannot establish 10 Hz or 250 ms. The\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.findings.md:258:10 Hz offered load even while the server owner is busy, A/B need independent\ncollab/jolt/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:211:Report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md\ncollab/jolt/1793027866046-engineer-j4d-local-persistence.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:28:- **Key files and signing:** keygen is 0600 and refuses overwrite; signing vectors are green.\ncollab/jolt/1793027866046-engineer-j4d-local-persistence.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:55:- **New entries:** `jolt_file_open_private` (O_WRONLY | O_CREAT | O_EXCL | O_CLOEXEC, **0600**: private from creation, the key-file requirement per F4, unlike HEAD's 0666 & ~uma