e p99 ≤ 250 ms and\ncollab/jolt/1792429520000-reviewer-jolt-j0b-udp-probe.glm-5.3.prompt.md:12:Output (under 600 words): verdict (SOUND / SOUND WITH CHANGES / UNSOUND), findings table (id, severity, file:line, evidence, correction), and what you could not verify. Cite file:line. Write ONLY: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792429520000-reviewer-jolt-j0b-udp-probe.glm-5.3.findings.md (same header fields). Do not enter plan mode.\ncollab/jolt/1793096000000-engineer-j6-autobahn-harness-prep.codex.prompt.md:27:   (the 500+ RFC 6455 cases) and the exception list format. If the\ncollab/jolt/1793096000000-engineer-j6-autobahn-harness-prep.codex.prompt.md:39:4. **The case triage**: the ~500 Autobahn cases partition into must-pass /\ncollab/jolt/1793096000000-engineer-j6-autobahn-harness-prep.codex.prompt.md:65:collab/1793096000000-engineer-j6-autobahn-harness-prep.codex.findings.md\ncollab/jolt/1792425688000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review-r5.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:31:| R3 | high | plan §6.1 item 3 (plan:148), \"Contract discrepancy\" (plan:152), J0 row (plan:227), J7 row (plan:234); `collab/1792423926000-…-r3.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md:17`; `src/cljc/dao/stream/datagram.cljc:25-33,294-300`; `docs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:141`; `docs/design/datom.world.md:70` | The only owner words quoted are \"yes, have the architect add the UDP probe to J0\" (plan:138). The text \"EAGAIN/full on send mapped to the dao.stream backpressure outcome\" first appears in the orchestrator's r3 brief (prompt:17). The plan nevertheless calls it \"the owner-requested probe full mapping … binding\". The landed contract excludes `:full` on purpose: \"this layer holds no outbound queue and a socket under pressure loses datagrams -- the medium's declared nature, not a refusal\" (`datagram.cljc:30-33`; doc :141). datom.world.md:70 says \"implementations do not add contracts\". Writing `:full` into J0 acceptance means the first commission would verify a contract that the landed design rejects. Item 4 has a related problem: \"send-would-block wait through the poller… then explicit retry\" puts an outbound wait under a contract with no queue, while `append!` is synchronous (`datagram.cljc:280-300`). | Remove \"owner-requested … binding\" unless the owner confirms the `:full` mapping in their own words. In J0, report EAGAIN on send as a distinct raw adapter result (for example `:would-block`), labelled injected or natural. At the contract surface, test the landed mapping: a clean `:dao.stream/transport-error` with a reason, nothing sent. Make send-side readiness waiting a probe-only observation, not adapter behavior. Turn \"should a UDP send that would block surface as `:full`, amending dao.stream.datagram.md?\" into an explicit owner question (Q7). J7 integrates whichever answer the owner gives. |\ncollab/jolt/1792429967000-engineer-jolt-j0b-udp-probe-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:94:  - A wait on the cancelled fd returned in `11/250` ms = 0.044 ms (:40). Other runs: `3/125` = 0.024 ms (run-5.log:40) and `29/500` = 0.058 ms (run-6.log:40).\ncollab/jolt/1792423926000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:160:- **(a) Generated ANTLR parsing worker — recommended completion path; host is a J5 parameter.** `yang.antlr.md:472–509` already specifies local-or-service parsing through streams. V: `yang.antlr.md:496–500,3229–3231` covers generated Python parsers for JVM, Node and Dart. `bb.edn:6–31` builds the Node bundle and Dart AOT peer; these prove available host targets, not an already implemented parsing-worker command. Qualify JVM / Node / Dart AOT over the same stream contract, defaulting to the target already a prerequisite of the lane being run. Among these choices, Dart AOT permits a JVM-free, Node-free deployed parser process tree (generation/build prerequisites remain separate). Use the pinned generated parser for that target and export the same sealed CST packets/diagnostics via the existing `yang.stage`/packet contracts. Keep scope/lowering/prelude/primitives/render/session evaluation in jolt. Also route the parser-dependent completeness probe through this worker or its equivalent diagnostic packet; otherwise multiline behavior diverges. One long-lived worker amortizes startup; no process per expression.\ncollab/jolt/1792423926000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:252:| F2 | Accepted | §§1, 7, J5, Q3: JVM/Node/Dart AOT worker parameter; generated-target evidence `yang.antlr.md:496–500,3229–3231`, builds `bb.edn:6–31`. |\ncollab/jolt/1792454716000-architect-jolt-design-doc-review.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md:10:Review /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md (1,735 lines; read all of it). It consolidates your r7 plan with owner decisions Q1-Q7, the CBOR-only WebSocket ruling, the shiva host, the confirmed defaults, licensing \"local builds only\" and ws-only, the J0b results, opus's r7 review (W1-W9) and Fable's four architect rulings (section 13.4: Transit kept off jolt via a shared predicate namespace plus an empty :jolt arm; WebSocket on jolt.socket.native + poller, never the shim; 1009 vs 1006 asserted per sender-declared wire behaviour; pin 96d7b866 kept at J0a). Compare against your r7 plan (collab/1792427226000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r7.gpt-6-astra.findings.md) and the opus r7 review (collab/1792427469000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review-r7.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md).\ncollab/jolt/1792454716000-architect-jolt-design-doc-review.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md:13:Output under 700 words: verdict (SIGNED OFF / SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES / NOT SIGNED OFF), findings table (id, severity, file:line of the document or repo, evidence, correction), and what you could not verify. Write ONLY /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792454716000-architect-jolt-design-doc-review.gpt-6-astra.findings.md (same header fields). Do not edit the design document. No src edits.\ncollab/jolt/1792422615171-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:35:| F2 | medium | plan §7 and §10 Q3 (`plan:138-140, 215`); `docs/design/yang.antlr.md:496-500, 3229-3231`; `bb.edn:28-31, 42-44`; `deps.edn:39, 86-91` | The plan's reading of yang.antlr.md is correct: §4.1 (`:472-509`) specifies a stream-based local-or-service parsing contract; `:3229` says no legacy fallback; `:4004-4006` records the legacy Python frontend deleted 2026-10-18; `src/cljc/yang/python.cljc` is indeed gone; `parser.cljc:18-22` imports generated Java classes under `:clj` and `frontends.cljc:15-17` requires it unconditionally, so removing one require does not fix the graph. Rejecting a new handwritten or CPython-AST parser is right. **However the option space is under-stated.** `yang.antlr.md:3230` and the table at `:496-500` say the Python grammar is generated for JVM, Node *and* Dart, and the repo already builds a Dart AOT native binary (`bb build:yin-repl-peer`, `bb.edn:28-31`) and a Node bundle (`build:yin-repl-node`) as lane prerequisites. A Node or Dart-AOT parse worker is the same stream contract with a non-JVM runtime, already validated on its own lane. Therefore Q3's sentence \"A no-JVM packaging requirement changes the parser implementation project\" is wrong: it changes which existing generated target the worker runs, a configuration choice, not a parser project. | In §7 make the worker host a J5 parameter (JVM / Node / Dart AOT) over one stream contract; recommend defaulting to whichever target is already a prerequisite of the lane being run, and note the Dart AOT peer binary is the only option that yields a JVM-free, Node-free process tree. Reword Q3 to ask which worker runtime(s) to qualify first, not whether a no-JVM requirement forces a new parser. |\ncollab/jolt/1792423156000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md:15:/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792423156000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\ncollab/jolt/1792490170000-reviewer-jolt-j0a-os-j0b-branch.qwen3.8-max.prompt.md:11:(1) /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.cl